# <%= it.name %>

<% if (it.description) { %><%= it.description %><% } else { %>A desktop app built with the DownDraft Engine.<% } %>

## Getting Started

```bash
# Install dependencies
bun install

# Run it (native winit + wgpu window)
npm run dev

# Package a distributable build
npm run release
```

## Project Structure

```
src/
  native-entry.ts  Desktop entry — window options, close policy, veto hook
  app-module.ts    The app: damage-driven renderer + html-ui document,
                   menus, dialogs, settings, second-instance handling
downdraft.config.json   appId, title, GPU mode
```

## Desktop features in this template

- **Damage-driven rendering** — `AppRenderer { mode:"2d", viewportCount:0, damageOnly:true }` idles at ~0 GPU; frames only render on change.
- **App menu** — `downdraft.setMenu` uses the OS menu on Windows/macOS and an in-window html-ui menu bar on Linux.
- **Native dialogs** — `downdraft.showOpenDialog` / `showSaveDialog` / `notify` / `showMessageBox`.
- **Settings** — `downdraft.settings` persists typed key/value state to `settings.json` in the app config dir (`downdraft.paths`).
- **Lifecycle** — `closePolicy`, vetoable `onCloseRequest`, and `onSecondInstance` forwarding in `src/native-entry.ts`.
- **Tray** — a commented `downdraft.tray` block in `app-module.ts` (pair with `closePolicy:"explicit"`).

Built with [DownDraft Engine](https://github.com/knackstedt/downdraft).
